---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Booke AI alternatives for bookkeeping firms — categorization & close"
  description="Looking past Booke AI’s $129/business layer on QBO/Xero? Compare Botkeeper, Digits, Double, Xenett, and Truewind for firm volume pricing, AI-native ledgers, or cheaper review. Pricing verified Oct 2026."
>
  <h1>Booke AI alternatives</h1>
  <p>Firms look beyond Booke AI when $129 per business/month adds up across many clients, when they need transparent firm/volume licenses or white-label without a sales quote, when they want an AI-native ledger instead of a layer on QuickBooks Online or Xero, or when the pain is review/close tooling more than daily bank coding. Below are the closest substitutes already in our directory — not a full market scan.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Alternative</th>
        <th>Best fit vs Booke AI</th>
        <th>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</th>
        <th>Trade-off</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/botkeeper`}>Botkeeper Infinite</a></td>
        <td>Closest firm-platform swap: AI categorization, recon, Close Tracker, Activity Hub on a license model</td>
        <td>From $149/license/mo (volume down to $59 at 25+)</td>
        <td>Fuller firm stack and volume tiers; higher list price at low client count vs Booke’s flat $129</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/digits`}>Digits</a></td>
        <td>AI-native general ledger with 24/7 bookkeeping and continuous recon — not a QBO/Xero add-on</td>
        <td>Per client: Essentials $65/mo, Core $100/mo, Pro $250/mo (US only; no seat fees)</td>
        <td>Clients leave QBO/Xero for Digits’ GL; US entities only</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/double`}>Double (formerly Keeper)</a></td>
        <td>Month-end close and client review layer on the existing QBO (and other) stack</td>
        <td>Per-client mix-and-match plans; demo required to start</td>
        <td>Close/review focus vs Booke’s daily categorization + doc matching; plan prices behind demo</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/xenett`}>Xenett</a></td>
        <td>AI financials review and firm workflow on QBO/Xero — flags P&amp;L and Balance Sheet issues</td>
        <td>AI Financials Review $7.50/client/mo; Workflow $10/client/mo (USD); add-ons e.g. Accruals + AI $15/client/mo</td>
        <td>Review/workflow layer, not daily bank-feed categorization or OCR document matching</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/truewind`}>Truewind</a></td>
        <td>AI bookkeeping and close on Sage Intacct or QBO — coding, recon, flux analysis</td>
        <td>By quote</td>
        <td>No published price card; sales-led vs Booke’s transparent Business tier</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>When to stay on Booke AI</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Clients must stay on QuickBooks Online or Xero; you want AI categorization, OCR, and exception review on top.</li>
    <li>You want a published per-business price ($129) before talking to sales; firm/white-label available by quote.</li>
    <li>Pain is daily bank coding, smart document matching, and missing-document chase — not firm-wide practice tooling.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When Botkeeper Infinite fits better</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You want Close Tracker, Activity Hub, and firm insights in one platform, not just a ledger layer.</li>
    <li>Volume license tiers ($149→$59) beat flat per-business pricing at your client count.</li>
    <li>Vendor risk is acceptable now that Infinite is operating again under Xendoo.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When Digits, Double, Xenett, or Truewind instead</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Digits: you’re willing to run US clients on an AI-native GL with per-client no-seat pricing.</li>
    <li>Double: close orchestration and AI transaction review on the existing ledger matter more than a published categorization card.</li>
    <li>Xenett: you need cheap, published review/workflow per client on QBO/Xero, not full daily AI bookkeeping.</li>
    <li>Truewind: close-complexity and Sage/QBO workflow depth matter more than a list price; expect a quote.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/compare/booke-ai-vs-botkeeper`}>Booke AI vs Botkeeper (head-to-head)</a>
